    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 4.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>Si curet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#IVAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.47"/> amicitiam ipsius porti, reddat nobis triginta sol. emendationis, si rex hoc concedat nobis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="74" ed="#robertson"/>Si curet<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IVAtr_4-2.robnote.fn.11"/> amicitiam ipsius porti, reddat nobis triginta sol. emendationis, si rex hoc concedat nobis.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ihm an der Freundschaft dieser Stadt [London] liegt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.1"/>, zahle er uns<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.2"/> 30 Schill. Busse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.3"/>, wenn der König uns dies zugestehen will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he cares about the friendship of this town [London], let him pay us 30 shillings in compensation, if the king will grant us this.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="75" ed="#robertson"/>If he values the good-will<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.1"/> of the town itself, he shall pay us<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.2"/> 30 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.3"/> as compensation, if the king will grant us this concession.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="235"><ref target="clause:Ine_9">Ine 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Ine 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="382"><ref target="clause:Duns_9-1">Duns 9.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Ine 9.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.47" n="47" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">curat <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">curat MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">recce freondscipes</hi> stand im Orig.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The orig. read <hi rend="italic">recce freondscipes</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Stadt London (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8. 54) spricht hier, wie VI As 8, 5 die Gilde, für eigene Kasse</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The town of London (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8. 54) speaks here, like the guild in VI As 8, 5, for its own coffers</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ich sehe hierin nicht mehr Ines Strafe für Pfändung in Selbsthilfe vór Aufforderung zum Rechtsgang, trotz wörtlichen Anklangs, sondern die Ungehorsamsbusse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 25), die dem Hundred oder Thegn zusteht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I no longer see in this Ine's penalty for distraint by self-help before a demand for legal process, despite the verbal echo, but rather the compensation for disobedience (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 25) that is due to the hundred or the thegn</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that the original text probably read <hi rend="italic">recce freondscipes</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the city authorities.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">It may be noted that the amount is the same as in the case of the (additional) fine paid to the hundred, see III Edm. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_4-2.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>curet</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">-at</hi> M, Hk.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
